sentences.l:
and he called to his companions,
looking at Ascalaphus and Aphareus and Deipyrus
and Meriones and Antilochus, masters of the battle-cry;

and I fear dreadfully
Aeneas coming on, swift in feet, who is coming at me,
who is very strong in battle men to slay;

And Aeneas from the other side called out to his own companions,
looking at Deiphobus and Paris and Agenor the heavenly,
who along with him leaders of the Trojans were;

and after that
the people followed, as when after the tame ram follow flocks
to drink, from the pasture;

and about their breasts the bronze
terribly rang, as they took aim through the throng
at one another;

And Idomeneus hit Oenomaus on the middle belly,
and broke the hollow of the breastplate, and through, the bowels, the bronze
drew out;

And Idomeneus from the corpse the long-shadowed spear
pulled out, nor besides that could he the other fair armour
from his shoulders take off;

until he came to the swift horses,
which for him behind the fight and the war
stood, having charioteer and intricate chariot;
